workedExamples.question_text:
Calculate the area of a circle with radius $4\text{ cm}$. Give the exact answer in terms of $\pi$, then round to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[black,thick] (0,0) circle (1.2);
\fill[black] (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[black] (0,0)--(40:1.2);
\path (40:0.65) node[above left,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the area of a circle with diameter $15\text{ m}$, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[black,thick] (0,0) circle (1.2);
\fill[black] (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[black] (-1.2,0)--(1.2,0);
\path (0,0) node[below,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$15\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

